"},"description":{"zh":"React 电子邮件是一个现代的、基于组件的电子邮件开发方法，使用 React 组件构建和发送 HTML 电子邮件","ja":"React 電子メールは、React コンポーネントを使用して HTML 電子メールをビルドして送信する、モダンなコンポーネントベースの電子メール開発方法です","ko":"React 이메일은 React 컴포넌트를 사용하여 HTML 이메일을 빌드하고 전송하는 모던한 컴포넌트 기반의 이메일 개발 방법입니다","es":"React Email es una herramienta para construir y enviar correos electrónicos HTML utilizando componentes de React","fr":"React Email est un outil pour créer et envoyer des emails HTML en utilisant des composants React","de":"React Email ist ein Tool zum Erstellen und Senden von HTML-E-Mails mithilfe von React-Komponenten","pt":"O React Email é uma abordagem moderna e baseada em componentes para o desenvolvimento de e-mails que funciona em todos os principais clientes de e-mail","ru":"React Email - это современный, компонентно-ориентированный подход к разработке электронных писем, который работает во всех основных клиентах электронной почты","ar":"React Email هو نهج حديث وقائم على المكونات لتنمية البريد الإلكتروني والذي يعمل على جميع عملاء البريد الإلكتروني الرئيسيين","en":"💌 Build and send emails using React"},"definition":{"en":"💌 Build and send emails using React"},"features":{"zh":["使用 React 组件构建电子邮件","支持所有主要电子邮件客户端","使用 create-email CLI 快速创建新项目","支持 npm、yarn、pnpm 和 bun 包管理器","提供样本电子邮件模板","现代的、基于组件的电子邮件开发方法"],"ja":["React コンポーネントを使用して電子メールをビルド","主要な電子メールクライアントをサポート","create-email CLI を使用して新規プロジェクトを迅速に作成","npm、yarn、pnpm、bun パッケージマネージャーをサポート","サンプル電子メールテンプレートを提供","モダンなコンポーネントベースの電子メール開発方法"],"ko":["React 컴포넌트를 사용하여 이메일을 빌드","주요 이메일 클라이언트를 지원","create-email CLI를 사용하여 새로운 프로젝트를 빠르게 생성","npm, yarn, pnpm, bun 패키지 관리자를 지원","샘플 이메일 템플릿을 제공","모던한 컴포넌트 기반의 이메일 개발 방법"],"es":["Crea correos electrónicos HTML personalizados","Utiliza componentes de React para construir correos electrónicos","Compatible con todos los principales clientes de correo electrónico","Fácil de instalar y configurar","Permite la creación de plantillas de correo electrónico personalizadas"],"fr":["Créez des emails HTML personnalisés","Utilisez des composants React pour créer des emails","Compatible avec tous les principaux clients de messagerie","Facile à installer et à configurer","Permet de créer des modèles d''email personnalisés"],"de":["Erstellen Sie benutzerdefinierte HTML-E-Mails","Verwenden Sie React-Komponenten, um E-Mails zu erstellen","Kompatibel mit allen wichtigen E-Mail-Clients","Einfach zu installieren und zu konfigurieren","Ermöglicht die Erstellung von benutzerdefinierten E-Mail-Vorlagen"],"pt":["Crie e-mails personalizados com componentes React","Funciona em todos os principais clientes de e-mail","Abordagem moderna e baseada em componentes","Instalação fácil com create-email CLI","Suporte a npm, yarn, pnpm e bun"],"ru":["Создавайте настраиваемые электронные письма с помощью компонентов React","Работает во всех основных клиентах электронной почты","Современный, компонентно-ориентированный подход","Легкая установка с помощью create-email CLI","Поддержка npm, yarn, pnpm и bun"],"ar":["انشئ رسائل بريد إلكتروني مخصصة باستخدام مكونات React","يعمل على جميع عملاء البريد الإلكتروني الرئيسيين","نهج حديث وقائم على المكونات","تثبيت سهل مع create-email CLI","دعم npm و yarn و pnpm و bun"]},"keywords":{"zh":["React 电子邮件","React 邮件","电子邮件开发","React 组件","HTML 电子邮件","create-email CLI","npm","yarn","pnpm","bun"],"ja":["React 電子メール","React メール","電子メール開発","React コンポーネント","HTML 電子メール","create-email CLI","npm","yarn","pnpm","bun"],"ko":["React 이메일","React 메일","이메일 개발","React 컴포넌트","HTML 이메일","create-email CLI","npm","yarn","pnpm","bun"],"es":["React Email","correo electrónico react","crear correos electrónicos con React","enviar correos electrónicos HTML","correo electrónico personalizado","react email template"],"fr":["React Email","email react","créer des emails avec React","envoyer des emails HTML","email personnalisé","modèle d''email react"],"de":["React Email","React E-Mail","Erstellen von E-Mails mit React","Senden von HTML-E-Mails","benutzerdefinierte E-Mail","React-E-Mail-Vorlage"],"pt":["React Email","Desenvolvimento de e-mails","Componentes React","E-mails personalizados","Create-email CLI","npm","yarn","pnpm","bun"],"ru":["React Email","Разработка электронных писем","Компоненты React","Настраиваемые электронные письма","Create-email CLI","npm","yarn","pnpm","bun"],"ar":["React Email","تنمية البريد الإلكتروني","مكونات React","البريد الإلكتروني المخصص","create-email CLI","npm","yarn","pnpm","bun"]}},"owner":"resend","repo":"react-email","repoPath":"resend/react-email","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-24T11:52:28.983Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"react-email","description":"Use when creating HTML email templates with React components - welcome emails, password resets, notifications, order confirmations, newsletters, or transactional emails.","version":"1.1.0","bodyPreview":"# React Email\n\nBuild and send HTML emails using React components - a modern, component-based approach to email development that works across all major email clients.\n\n## Installation\n\nYou need to scaffold a new React Email project using the create-email CLI. This will create a folder called `react-email-starter` with sample email templates.\n\nUsing npm:\n```sh\nnpx create-email@latest\n```\n\nUsing yarn:\n```sh\nyarn create email\n```\n\nUsing pnpm:\n```sh\npnpm create email\n```\n\nUsing bun:\n```sh\nbun create","body":"# React Email\n\nBuild and send HTML emails using React components - a modern, component-based approach to email development that works across all major email clients.\n\n## Installation\n\nYou need to scaffold a new React Email project using the create-email CLI. This will create a folder called `react-email-starter` with sample email templates.\n\nUsing npm:\n```sh\nnpx create-email@latest\n```\n\nUsing yarn:\n```sh\nyarn create email\n```\n\nUsing pnpm:\n```sh\npnpm create email\n```\n\nUsing bun:\n```sh\nbun create email\n```\n\n## Navigate to Project Directory\n\nYou must change into the newly created project folder:\n\n```sh\ncd react-email-starter\n```\n\n## Install Dependencies\n\nYou need to install all project dependencies before running the development server.\n\nUsing npm:\n```sh\nnpm install\n```\n\nUsing yarn:\n```sh\nyarn\n```\n\nUsing pnpm:\n```sh\npnpm install\n```\n\nUsing bun:\n```sh\nbun install\n```\n\n## Start the Development Server\n\nYour task is to start the local preview server to view and edit email templates.\n\nUsing npm:\n```sh\nnpm run dev\n```\n\nUsing yarn:\n```sh\nyarn dev\n```\n\nUsing pnpm:\n```sh\npnpm dev\n```\n\nUsing bun:\n```sh\nbun dev\n```\n\n## Verify Installation\n\nConfirm the development server is running by checking that localhost:3000 is accessible. The server will display a preview interface where you can view email templates from the `emails` folder.\n\n### Notes on installation\nAssuming React Email is installed in an existing project, update the top-level package.json file with a script to run the React Email preview server.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"email\": \"email dev --dir emails --port 3000\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\nMake sure the path to the emails folder is relative to the base project directory.\n\n\n### tsconfig.json updating or creation\n\nEnsure the tsconfig.json includes proper support for jsx.\n\n## Basic Email Template\n\nReplace the sample email templates. Here is how to create a new email template:\n\nCreate an email component with proper structure using the Tailwind component for styling:\n\n```tsx\nimport {\n  Html,\n  Head,\n  Preview,\n  Body,\n  Container,\n  Heading,\n  Text,\n  Button,\n  Tailwind,\n  pixelBasedPreset\n} from ''@react-email/components'';\n\ninterface WelcomeEmailProps {\n  name: string;\n  verificationUrl: string;\n}\n\nexport default function WelcomeEmail({ name, verificationUrl }: WelcomeEmailProps) {\n  return (\n    <Html lang=\"en\">\n      <Tailwind\n        config={{\n          presets: [pixelBasedPreset],\n          theme: {\n            extend: {\n              colors: {\n                brand: ''#007bff'',\n              },\n            },\n          },\n        }}\n      >\n        <Head />\n        <Preview>Welcome - Verify your email</Preview>\n        <Body className=\"bg-gray-100 font-sans\">\n          <Container className=\"max-w-xl mx-auto p-5\">\n            <Heading className=\"text-2xl text-gray-800\">\n              Welcome!\n            </Heading>\n            <Text className=\"text-base text-gray-800\">\n              Hi {name}, thanks for signing up!\n            </Text>\n            <Button\n              href={verificationUrl}\n              className=\"bg-brand text-white px-5 py-3 rounded block text-center no-underline\"\n            >\n              Verify Email\n            </Button>\n          </Container>\n        </Body>\n      </Tailwind>\n    </Html>\n  );\n}\n\n// Preview props for testing\nWelcomeEmail.PreviewProps = {\n  name: ''John Doe'',\n  verificationUrl: ''https://example.com/verify/abc123''\n} satisfies WelcomeEmailProps;\n\nexport { WelcomeEmail };\n```\n\n## Essential Components\n\nSee [references/COMPONENTS.md](references/COMPONENTS.md) for complete component documentation.\n\n**Core Structure:**\n- `Html` - Root wrapper with `lang` attribute\n- `Head` - Meta elements, styles, fonts\n- `Body` - Main content wrapper\n- `Container` - Centers content (max-width layout)\n- `Section` - Layout sections\n- `Row` & `Column` - Multi-column layouts\n- `Tailwind` - Enables Tailwind CSS utility classes\n\n**Content:**\n- `Preview` - Inbox preview text, always first in `Body`\n- `Heading` - h1-h6 headings\n- `Text` - Paragraphs\n- `Button` - Styled link buttons\n- `Link` - Hyperlinks\n- `Img` - Images (see Static Files section below)\n- `Hr` - Horizontal dividers\n\n**Specialized:**\n- `CodeBlock` - Syntax-highlighted code\n- `CodeInline` - Inline code\n- `Markdown` - Render markdown\n- `Font` - Custom web fonts\n\n## Before Writing Code\n\nWhen a user requests an email template, ask clarifying questions FIRST if they haven''t provided:\n\n1. **Brand colors** - Ask for primary brand color (hex code like #007bff)\n2. **Logo** - Ask if they have a logo file and its format (PNG/JPG only - warn if SVG/WEBP)\n3. **Style preference** - Professional, casual, or minimal tone\n4. **Production URL** - Where will static assets be hosted in production?\n\nExample response to vague request:\n> Before I create your email template, I have a few questions:\n> 1. What is your primary brand color? (hex code)\n> 2. Do you have a logo file? (PNG or JPG - note: SVG and WEBP don''t work reliably in email clients)\n> 3. What tone do you prefer - professional, casual, or minimal?\n> 4. Where will you host static assets in production? (e.g., https://cdn.example.com)\n\n## Static Files and Images\n\n### Directory Structure\n\nLocal images must be placed in the `static` folder inside your emails directory:\n\n```\nproject/\n├── emails/\n│   ├── welcome.tsx\n│   └── static/           <-- Images go here\n│       └── logo.png\n```\n\nIf user has an image elsewhere, instruct them to copy it:\n```sh\ncp ./assets/logo.png ./emails/static/logo.png\n```\n\n### Dev vs Production URLs\n\nUse this pattern for images that work in both dev preview and production:\n\n```tsx\nconst baseURL = process.env.NODE_ENV === \"production\"\n  ? \"https://cdn.example.com\"  // User''s production CDN\n  : \"\";\n\nexport default function Email() {\n  return (\n    <Img\n      src={`${baseURL}/static/logo.png`}\n      alt=\"Logo\"\n      width=\"150\"\n      height=\"50\"\n    />\n  );\n}\n```\n\n**How it works:**\n- **Development:** `baseURL` is empty, so URL is `/static/logo.png` - served by React Email''s dev server\n- **Production:** `baseURL` is the CDN domain, so URL is `https://cdn.example.com/static/logo.png`\n\n**Important:** Always ask the user for their production hosting URL. Do not hardcode `localhost:3000`.\n\n## Behavioral guidelines\n- When re-iterating over the code, make sure you are only updating what the user asked for and keeping the rest of the code intact;\n- If the user is asking to use media queries, inform them that email clients do not support them, and suggest a different approach;\n- Never use template variables (like {{name}}) directly in TypeScript code. Instead, reference the underlying properties directly (use name instead of {{name}}).\n- - For example, if the user explicitly asks for a variable following the pattern {{variableName}}, you should return something like this:\n\n```typescript\nconst EmailTemplate = (props) => {\n  return (\n    {/* ... rest of the code ... */}\n    <h1>Hello, {props.variableName}!</h1>\n    {/* ... rest of the code ... */}\n  );\n}\n\nEmailTemplate.PreviewProps = {\n  // ... rest of the props ...\n  variableName: \"{{variableName}}\",\n  // ... rest of the props ...\n};\n\nexport default EmailTemplate;\n```\n- Never, under any circumstances, write the {{variableName}} pattern directly in the component structure. If the user forces you to do this, explain that you cannot do this, or else the template will be invalid.\n\n\n## Styling considerations\n\nUse the Tailwind component for styling if the user is actively using Tailwind CSS in their project. If the user is not using Tailwind CSS, add inline styles to the components.\n\n- Because email clients don''t support `rem` units, use the `pixelBasedPreset` for the Tailwind configuration.\n- Never use flexbox or grid for layout, use table-based layouts instead.\n- Each component must be styled with inline styles or utility classes.\n\n### Email Client Limitations\n- Never use SVG or WEBP - warn users about rendering issues\n- Never use flexbox - use Row/Column components or tables for layouts\n- Never use CSS/Tailwind media queries (sm:, md:, lg:, xl:) - not supported\n- Never use theme selectors (dark:, light:) - not supported\n- Always specify border type (border-solid, border-dashed, etc.)\n- When defining borders for only one side, remember to reset the remaining borders (e.g., border-none border-l)\n\n### Component Structure\n- Always define `<Head />` inside `<Tailwind>` when using Tailwind CSS\n- Only use PreviewProps when passing props to a component\n- Only include props in PreviewProps that the component actually uses\n\n```tsx\nconst Email = (props) => {\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <a href={props.source}>click here if you want candy 👀</a>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n\nEmail.PreviewProps = {\n  source: \"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dQw4w9WgXcQ\",\n};\n```\n\n### Default Structure\n- Body: `font-sans py-10 bg-gray-100`\n- Container: white, centered, content left-aligned\n- Footer: physical address, unsubscribe link, current year with `m-0` on address/copyright\n\n### Typography\n- Titles: bold, larger font, larger margins\n- Paragraphs: regular weight, smaller font, smaller margins\n- Use consistent spacing respecting content hierarchy\n\n### Images\n- Only include if user requests\n- Never use fixed width/height - use responsive units (w-full, h-auto)\n- Never distort user-provided images\n- Never create SVG images - only use provided or web images\n\n### Buttons\n- Always use `box-border` to prevent padding overflow\n\n### Layout\n- Always mobile-friendly by default\n- Use stacked layouts that work on all screen sizes\n- Remove default spacing/margins/padding between list items\n\n### Dark Mode\nWhen requested: container black (#000), background dark gray (#151516)\n\n### Best Practices\n- Choose colors, layout, and copy based on user''s request\n- Make templates unique, not generic\n- Use keywords in email body to increase conversion\n\n## Rendering\n\n### Convert to HTML\n\n```tsx\nimport { render } from ''@react-email/components'';\nimport { WelcomeEmail } from ''./emails/welcome'';\n\nconst html = await render(\n  <WelcomeEmail name=\"John\" verificationUrl=\"https://example.com/verify\" />\n);\n```\n\n### Convert to Plain Text\n\n```tsx\nimport { render } from ''@react-email/components'';\nimport { WelcomeEmail } from ''./emails/welcome'';\n\nconst text = await render(<WelcomeEmail name=\"John\" verificationUrl=\"https://example.com/verify\" />, { plainText: true });\n```\n\n## Sending\n\nReact Email supports sending with any email service provider. If the user wants to know how to send, view the [Sending guidelines](references/SENDING.md).\n\nQuick example using the Resend SDK for Node.js:\n\n```tsx\nimport { Resend } from ''resend'';\nimport { WelcomeEmail } from ''./emails/welcome'';\n\nconst resend = new Resend(process.env.RESEND_API_KEY);\n\nconst { data, error } = await resend.emails.send({\n  from: ''Acme <onboarding@resend.dev>'',\n  to: [''user@example.com''],\n  subject: ''Welcome to Acme'',\n  react: <WelcomeEmail name=\"John\" verificationUrl=\"https://example.com/verify\" />\n});\n\nif (error) {\n  console.error(''Failed to send:'', error);\n}\n```\n\nThe Node SDK automatically handles the plain-text rendering and HTML rendering for you.\n\n## Internationalization\n\nSee [references/I18N.md](references/I18N.md) for complete i18n documentation.\n\nReact Email supports three i18n libraries: next-intl, react-i18next, and react-intl.\n\n### Quick Example (next-intl)\n\n```tsx\nimport { createTranslator } from ''next-intl'';\nimport {\n  Html,\n  Body,\n  Container,\n  Text,\n  Button,\n  Tailwind,\n  pixelBasedPreset\n} from ''@react-email/components'';\n\ninterface EmailProps {\n  name: string;\n  locale: string;\n}\n\nexport default async function WelcomeEmail({ name, locale }: EmailProps) {\n  const t = createTranslator({\n    messages: await import(\\`../messages/\\${locale}.json\\`),\n    namespace: ''welcome-email'',\n    locale\n  });\n\n  return (\n    <Html lang={locale}>\n      <Tailwind config={{ presets: [pixelBasedPreset] }}>\n        <Body className=\"bg-gray-100 font-sans\">\n          <Container className=\"max-w-xl mx-auto p-5\">\n            <Text className=\"text-base text-gray-800\">{t(''greeting'')} {name},</Text>\n            <Text className=\"text-base text-gray-800\">{t(''body'')}</Text>\n            <Button href=\"https://example.com\" className=\"bg-blue-600 text-white px-5 py-3 rounded\">\n              {t(''cta'')}\n            </Button>\n          </Container>\n        </Body>\n      </Tailwind>\n    </Html>\n  );\n}\n```\n\nMessage files (\\`messages/en.json\\`, \\`messages/es.json\\`, etc.):\n\n```json\n{\n  \"welcome-email\": {\n    \"greeting\": \"Hi\",\n    \"body\": \"Thanks for signing up!\",\n    \"cta\": \"Get Started\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Email Best Practices\n\n1. **Test across email clients** - Test in Gmail, Outlook, Apple Mail, Yahoo Mail. Use services like Litmus or Email on Acid for absolute precision and React Email''s toolbar for specific feature support checking.\n\n2. **Keep it responsive** - Max-width around 600px, test on mobile devices.\n\n3. **Use absolute image URLs** - Host on reliable CDN, always include \\`alt\\` text.\n\n4. **Provide plain text version** - Required for accessibility and some email clients.\n\n5. **Keep file size under 102KB** - Gmail clips larger emails.\n\n6. **Add proper TypeScript types** - Define interfaces for all email props.\n\n7. **Include preview props** - Add \\`.PreviewProps\\` to components for development testing.\n\n8. **Handle errors** - Always check for errors when sending emails.\n\n9.  **Use verified domains** - For production, use verified domains in \\`from\\` addresses.\n\n## Common Patterns\n\nSee [references/PATTERNS.md](references/PATTERNS.md) for complete examples including:\n- Password reset emails\n- Order confirmations with product lists\n- Notification emails with code blocks\n- Multi-column layouts\n- Email templates with custom fonts\n\n## Additional Resources\n\n- [React Email Documentation](https://react.email/docs/llms.txt)\n- [React Email GitHub](https://github.com/resend/react-email)\n- [Resend Documentation](https://resend.com/docs/llms.txt)\n- [Email Client CSS Support](https://www.caniemail.com)\n- Component Reference: [references/COMPONENTS.md](references/COMPONENTS.md)\n- Internationalization Guide: [references/I18N.md](references/I18N.md)\n- Common Patterns: [references/PATTERNS.md](references/PATTERNS.md)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-24T11:56:29.888Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Frontend Agents needing to build and send dynamic HTML emails using React components","zh":"非常适合需要使用 React 组件构建和发送动态 HTML 电子邮件的前端代理","ja":"React コンポーネントを使用して動的な HTML 電子メールを構築および送信する必要があるフロントエンド エージェントに最適","ko":"리액트 컴포넌트를 사용하여 동적인 HTML 이메일을 구축 및 전송해야 하는 프론트엔드 에이전트에 적합","es":"Perfecto para agentes de frontend que necesitan construir y enviar correos electrónicos HTML dinámicos utilizando componentes de React","fr":"Parfait pour les agents frontend qui ont besoin de créer et d''envoyer des e-mails HTML dynamiques à l''aide de composants React","de":"Perfekt für Frontend-Agents, die dynamische HTML-E-Mails mit React-Komponenten erstellen und senden müssen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Frontend que precisam construir e enviar e-mails dinâmicos em HTML usando componentes React","ru":"Идеально для фронтенд-агентов, которым необходимо создавать и отправлять динамические электронные письма в формате HTML, используя компоненты React","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الأماميين الذين يحتاجون إلى بناء وارسال رسائل بريد إلكتروني ديناميكية في HTML باستخدام مكونات React"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to generate and send HTML emails across all major email clients using React components, leveraging create-email CLI for scaffolding and supporting package managers like npm, yarn, pnpm, and bun","zh":"赋予代理生成和发送所有主要电子邮件客户端的 HTML 电子邮件的能力，使用 React 组件，利用 create-email CLI 进行脚手架搭建，并支持像 npm、yarn、pnpm 和 bun这样的包管理器","ja":"create-email CLI を使用してスケルトンを作成し、npm、yarn、pnpm、bun などのパッケージ マネージャーをサポートすることで、React コンポーネントを使用してすべてのメジャー電子メール クライアントで HTML 電子メールを生成および送信するエージェントの能力を提供する","ko":"create-email CLI를 사용하여 스켈레톤을 생성하고 npm, yarn, pnpm, bunなどの 패키지 매니저를 지원함으로써 에이전트가 모든 주요 이메일 클라이언트에서 HTML 이메일을 생성 및 전송할 수 있는 능력을 제공하는 리액트 컴포넌트","es":"Permite a los agentes generar y enviar correos electrónicos HTML en todos los clientes de correo electrónico principales utilizando componentes de React, aprovechando create-email CLI para la creación del esqueleto del proyecto y admitiendo administradores de paquetes como npm, yarn, pnpm y bun","fr":"Permet aux agents de générer et d''envoyer des e-mails HTML sur tous les principaux clients de messagerie à l''aide de composants React, en exploitant create-email CLI pour le squelette du projet et en prenant en charge les gestionnaires de paquets tels que npm, yarn, pnpm et bun","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, HTML-E-Mails mit React-Komponenten über alle wichtigen E-Mail-Clients zu generieren und zu senden, indem create-email CLI für das Projekt-Skelett verwendet wird und Paket-Manager wie npm, yarn, pnpm und bun unterstützt werden","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerar e enviar e-mails em HTML em todos os principais clientes de e-mail usando componentes React, aproveitando o create-email CLI para estruturação e suportando gerenciadores de pacotes como npm, yarn, pnpm e bun","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью генерировать и отправлять электронные письма в формате HTML во всех основных клиентах электронной почты, используя компоненты React, используя create-email CLI для создания каркаса и поддерживая менеджеры пакетов, такие как npm, yarn, pnpm и bun","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على توليد وارسال رسائل بريد إلكتروني في HTML عبر جميع العملاء الرئيسيين لبريد الإلكترون باستخدام مكونات React، واستخدام create-email CLI للهيكلة ودعم المديرين الحزمة مثل npm و yarn و pnpm و bun"},"useCases":{"en":["Building responsive email templates","Sending automated emails using React components","Creating customizable email campaigns"],"zh":["构建响应式电子邮件模板","使用 React 组件发送自动电子邮件","创建可自定义的电子邮件活动"],"ja":["レスポンシブ電子メールテンプレートの構築","React コンポーネントを使用した自動電子メールの送信","カスタマイズ可能な電子メールキャンペーンの作成"],"ko":["반응형 이메일 템플릿 구축","리액트 컴포넌트를 사용한 자동 이메일 전송","사용자 정의 가능한 이메일 캠페인 생성"],"es":["Creación de plantillas de correo electrónico responsivas","Envío de correos electrónicos automatizados utilizando componentes de React","Creación de campañas de correo electrónico personalizables"],"fr":["Création de modèles d''e-mail responsives","Envoi d''e-mails automatisés à l''aide de composants React","Création de campagnes d''e-mail personnalisables"],"de":["Erstellung responsiver E-Mail-Vorlagen","Senden automatisierter E-Mails mit React-Komponenten","Erstellung anpassbarer E-Mail-Kampagnen"],"pt":["Construir modelos de e-mail responsivos","Enviar e-mails automatizados usando componentes React","Criar campanhas de e-mail personalizáveis"],"ru":["Создание адаптивных шаблонов электронной почты","Отправка автоматических электронных писем, используя компоненты React","Создание настраиваемых электронных кампаний"],"ar":["بناء نماذج رسائل البريد الإلكتروني المستجيبة","إرسال رسائل بريد إلكتروني آلية باستخدام مكونات React","إنشاء حملات بريد إلكتروني قابلة للتعديل"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires create-email CLI for project scaffolding","Limited to email clients that support HTML emails"],"zh":["需要 create-email CLI 进行项目脚手架搭建","仅限于支持 HTML 电子邮件的电子邮件客户端"],"ja":["プロジェクト スケルトン作成には create-email CLI が必要","HTML 電子メールをサポートする電子メール クライアントに限定される"],"ko":["프로젝트 스켈레톤 생성을 위해 create-email CLI가 필요","HTML 이메일을 지원하는 이메일 클라이언트로 제한"],"es":["Requiere create-email CLI para la creación del esqueleto del proyecto","Limitado a clientes de correo electrónico que soportan correos electrónicos HTML"],"fr":["Nécessite create-email CLI pour le squelette du projet","Limité aux clients de messagerie qui prennent en charge les e-mails HTML"],"de":["Benötigt create-email CLI für das Projekt-Skelett","Begrenzt auf E-Mail-Clients, die HTML-E-Mails unterstützen"],"pt":["Requer create-email CLI para estruturação do projeto","Limitado a clientes de e-mail que suportam e-mails em HTML"],"ru":["Требуется create-email CLI для создания каркаса проекта","Ограничен клиентами электронной почты, которые поддерживают электронные письма в формате HTML"],"ar":["يتطلب create-email CLI لهيكلة المشروع","محدود للعملاء الذين يدعمون رسائل البريد الإلكتروني في HTML"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"188d1556f5601bd3dbd9f0e57f9cbba9cbd7fad1ff75a1597fa7cbe7f15a73c6","qualityScore":45}');
