,"النوع","الأخطاء الشائعة","إنتاجية المطور"]}},"owner":"actionbook","repo":"rust-skills","repoPath":"actionbook/rust-skills","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-20T04:13:19.577Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"m04-zero-cost","description":"CRITICAL: Use for generics, traits, zero-cost abstraction. Triggers: E0277, E0308, E0599, generic, trait, impl, dyn, where, monomorphization, static dispatch, dynamic dispatch, impl Trait, trait bound not satisfied, 泛型, 特征, 零成本抽象, 单态化","bodyPreview":"# Zero-Cost Abstraction\n\n> **Layer 1: Language Mechanics**\n\n## Core Question\n\n**Do we need compile-time or runtime polymorphism?**\n\nBefore choosing between generics and trait objects:\n- Is the type known at compile time?\n- Is a heterogeneous collection needed?\n- What''s the performance priority?\n\n---\n\n## Error → Design Question\n\n| Error | Don''t Just Say | Ask Instead |\n|-------|----------------|-------------|\n| E0277 | \"Add trait bound\" | Is this abstraction at the right level? |\n| E0308 | \"Fix t","body":"# Zero-Cost Abstraction\n\n> **Layer 1: Language Mechanics**\n\n## Core Question\n\n**Do we need compile-time or runtime polymorphism?**\n\nBefore choosing between generics and trait objects:\n- Is the type known at compile time?\n- Is a heterogeneous collection needed?\n- What''s the performance priority?\n\n---\n\n## Error → Design Question\n\n| Error | Don''t Just Say | Ask Instead |\n|-------|----------------|-------------|\n| E0277 | \"Add trait bound\" | Is this abstraction at the right level? |\n| E0308 | \"Fix the type\" | Should types be unified or distinct? |\n| E0599 | \"Import the trait\" | Is the trait the right abstraction? |\n| E0038 | \"Make object-safe\" | Do we really need dynamic dispatch? |\n\n---\n\n## Thinking Prompt\n\nBefore adding trait bounds:\n\n1. **What abstraction is needed?**\n   - Same behavior, different types → trait\n   - Different behavior, same type → enum\n   - No abstraction needed → concrete type\n\n2. **When is type known?**\n   - Compile time → generics (static dispatch)\n   - Runtime → trait objects (dynamic dispatch)\n\n3. **What''s the trade-off priority?**\n   - Performance → generics\n   - Compile time → trait objects\n   - Flexibility → depends\n\n---\n\n## Trace Up ↑\n\nWhen type system fights back:\n\n```\nE0277 (trait bound not satisfied)\n    ↑ Ask: Is the abstraction level correct?\n    ↑ Check: m09-domain (what behavior is being abstracted?)\n    ↑ Check: m05-type-driven (should use newtype?)\n```\n\n| Persistent Error | Trace To | Question |\n|-----------------|----------|----------|\n| Complex trait bounds | m09-domain | Is the abstraction right? |\n| Object safety issues | m05-type-driven | Can typestate help? |\n| Type explosion | m10-performance | Accept dyn overhead? |\n\n---\n\n## Trace Down ↓\n\nFrom design to implementation:\n\n```\n\"Need to abstract over types with same behavior\"\n    ↓ Types known at compile time → impl Trait or generics\n    ↓ Types determined at runtime → dyn Trait\n\n\"Need collection of different types\"\n    ↓ Closed set → enum\n    ↓ Open set → Vec<Box<dyn Trait>>\n\n\"Need to return different types\"\n    ↓ Same type → impl Trait\n    ↓ Different types → Box<dyn Trait>\n```\n\n---\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Pattern | Dispatch | Code Size | Runtime Cost |\n|---------|----------|-----------|--------------|\n| `fn foo<T: Trait>()` | Static | +bloat | Zero |\n| `fn foo(x: &dyn Trait)` | Dynamic | Minimal | vtable lookup |\n| `impl Trait` return | Static | +bloat | Zero |\n| `Box<dyn Trait>` | Dynamic | Minimal | Allocation + vtable |\n\n## Syntax Comparison\n\n```rust\n// Static dispatch - type known at compile time\nfn process(x: impl Display) { }      // argument position\nfn process<T: Display>(x: T) { }     // explicit generic\nfn get() -> impl Display { }         // return position\n\n// Dynamic dispatch - type determined at runtime\nfn process(x: &dyn Display) { }      // reference\nfn process(x: Box<dyn Display>) { }  // owned\n```\n\n## Error Code Reference\n\n| Error | Cause | Quick Fix |\n|-------|-------|-----------|\n| E0277 | Type doesn''t impl trait | Add impl or change bound |\n| E0308 | Type mismatch | Check generic params |\n| E0599 | No method found | Import trait with `use` |\n| E0038 | Trait not object-safe | Use generics or redesign |\n\n---\n\n## Decision Guide\n\n| Scenario | Choose | Why |\n|----------|--------|-----|\n| Performance critical | Generics | Zero runtime cost |\n| Heterogeneous collection | `dyn Trait` | Different types at runtime |\n| Plugin architecture | `dyn Trait` | Unknown types at compile |\n| Reduce compile time | `dyn Trait` | Less monomorphization |\n| Small, known type set | `enum` | No indirection |\n\n---\n\n## Object Safety\n\nA trait is object-safe if it:\n- Doesn''t have `Self: Sized` bound\n- Doesn''t return `Self`\n- Doesn''t have generic methods\n- Uses `where Self: Sized` for non-object-safe methods\n\n---\n\n## Anti-Patterns\n\n| Anti-Pattern | Why Bad | Better |\n|--------------|---------|--------|\n| Over-generic everything | Compile time, complexity | Concrete types when possible |\n| `dyn` for known types | Unnecessary indirection | Generics |\n| Complex trait hierarchies | Hard to understand | Simpler design |\n| Ignore object safety | Limits flexibility | Plan for dyn if needed |\n\n---\n\n## Related Skills\n\n| When | See |\n|------|-----|\n| Type-driven design | m05-type-driven |\n| Domain abstraction | m09-domain |\n| Performance concerns | m10-performance |\n| Send/Sync bounds | m07-concurrency |\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-20T04:50:05.206Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Rust Developer Agents needing advanced compile-time and runtime polymorphism decision-making capabilities.","zh":"适用于需要高级编译时和运行时多态决策能力的Rust开发者代理。","ja":"Rust開発者エージェントが高度なコンパイル時とランタイムの多相性の意思決定能力を必要とする場合に適しています。","ko":"고급 컴파일 타임 및 런타임 다형성 의사 결정 기능이 필요한 Rust 개발자 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Desarrollo de Rust que necesitan capacidades de toma de decisiones de polimorfismo en tiempo de compilación y ejecución avanzadas.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents de Développement Rust qui ont besoin de capacités de prise de décision de polymorphisme à temps de compilation et d''exécution avancées.","de":"Perfekt für Rust-Entwicklungsagenten, die erweiterte Entscheidungskapazitäten für Compile-Time- und Laufzeitpolymorphismus benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvedores Rust que precisam de capacidades avançadas de tomada de decisão de polimorfismo em tempo de compilação e execução.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработчиков Rust, которым необходимы расширенные возможности принятия решений по полиморфизму во время компиляции и выполнения.","ar":"مثالي لعميل مطور روست الذي يحتاج إلى قدرات متقدمة في اتخاذ قرارات متعددة الشكل في وقت الترجمة ووقت التشغيل."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to make informed decisions between generics and trait objects, considering performance priorities and heterogeneous collection needs, using Rust''s type system and trait bounds, and resolving errors like E0277 and E0308 with targeted design questions.","zh":"赋予代理在Rust的类型系统和特征边界的基础上，权衡性能优先级和异构集合需求之间做出明智的决定，并使用有针对性的设计问题解决诸如E0277和E0308等错误。","ja":"Rustの型システムと特性の境界を使用して、エージェントがパフォーマンスの優先順位と異種コレクションのニーズのバランスをとる決定を下し、E0277およびE0308などのエラーを対象としたデザインの質問で解決することを可能にします。","ko":"에이전트가 런타임과 컴파일 타임의 다형성을 결정하기 위해 Rust의 타입 시스템과 특성 경계를 사용하여 성능 우선순위와 이질적 컬렉션 요구 사항 사이에서 정보에 기반한 결정을 내릴 수 있도록 하며, E0277 및 E0308과 같은 오류를 해결하기 위한 대상 설계 질문을 사용합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a tomar decisiones informadas entre genéricos y objetos de rasgos, considerando prioridades de rendimiento y necesidades de colecciones heterogéneas, utilizando el sistema de tipos de Rust y los límites de rasgos, y resolviendo errores como E0277 y E0308 con preguntas de diseño dirigidas.","fr":"Permet aux agents de prendre des décisions éclairées entre les génériques et les objets de traits, en tenant compte des priorités de performances et des besoins de collections hétérogènes, en utilisant le système de types de Rust et les limites de traits, et en résolvant les erreurs comme E0277 et E0308 avec des questions de conception ciblées.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, fundierte Entscheidungen zwischen Generics und Trait-Objekten zu treffen, unter Berücksichtigung von LeistungsPrioritäten und Bedürfnissen heterogener Sammlungen, unter Verwendung von Rusts Typsystem und Trait-Grenzen undAuflösung von Fehlern wie E0277 und E0308 mit gezielten Designfragen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a tomar decisões informadas entre genéricos e objetos de traço, considerando prioridades de desempenho e necessidades de coleções heterogêneas, usando o sistema de tipos do Rust e os limites de traço, e resolvendo erros como E0277 e E0308 com questões de design direcionadas.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью принимать обоснованные решения между泛型ами и объектами трейтов, учитывая приоритеты производительности и потребности в гетерогенных коллекциях, используя систему типов Rust и ограничения трейтов, и решая ошибки, такие как E0277 и E0308, с помощью целенаправленных вопросов дизайна.","ar":"تمكّن الوكيل من اتخاذ قرارات مدروسة بين العموميات وكائنات السمة، مع مراعاة أولويات الأداء واحتياجات المجموعات المتنوعة، باستخدام نظام أنواع روست وحدود السمات، وحل الأخطاء مثل E0277 و E0308 باستخدام أسئلة التصميم المستهدفة."},"useCases":{"en":["Determining the need for compile-time or runtime polymorphism in Rust code","Resolving errors related to trait bounds and object safety","Optimizing Rust code for performance by choosing the right abstraction level"],"zh":["确定Rust代码中编译时或运行时多态性的需求","解决与特征边界和对象安全性相关的错误","通过选择合适的抽象级别来优化Rust代码的性能"],"ja":["Rustコードにおけるコンパイル時の多相性またはランタイムの多相性の必要性を決定する","特性の境界とオブジェクトの安全性に関連するエラーを解決する","抽象レベルの最適な選択によってRustコードのパフォーマンスを最適化する"],"ko":["Rust 코드에서 컴파일 타임 또는 런타임 다형성의 필요성을 결정하는こと","특성 경계 및 객체 안전성과 관련된 오류를 해결하는 것","적절한 추상화 수준을 선택하여 Rust 코드의 성능을 최적화하는 것"],"es":["Determinar la necesidad de polimorfismo en tiempo de compilación o ejecución en el código Rust","Resolver errores relacionados con los límites de rasgos y la seguridad de los objetos","Optimizar el código Rust para el rendimiento eligiendo el nivel de abstracción adecuado"],"fr":["Déterminer la nécessité de polymorphisme à temps de compilation ou d''exécution dans le code Rust","Résoudre les erreurs liées aux limites de traits et à la sécurité des objets","Optimiser le code Rust pour les performances en choisissant le bon niveau d''abstraction"],"de":["Feststellen des Bedarfs an Compile-Time- oder Laufzeitpolymorphismus in Rust-Code","Auflösen von Fehlern im Zusammenhang mit Trait-Grenzen und Objektsicherheit","Optimieren von Rust-Code für die Leistung durch Auswahl des richtigen Abstraktionsniveaus"],"pt":["Determinar a necessidade de polimorfismo em tempo de compilação ou execução no código Rust","Resolver erros relacionados a limites de traço e segurança de objeto","Otimizar o código Rust para desempenho, escolhendo o nível de abstração correto"],"ru":["Определение необходимости полиморфизма во время компиляции или выполнения в коде Rust","Решение ошибок, связанных с ограничениями трейтов и безопасностью объектов","Оптимизация кода Rust для производительности путем выбора правильного уровня абстракции"],"ar":["تحديد الحاجة إلى متعدد الشكل في وقت الترجمة أو وقت التشغيل في رمز روست","حل الأخطاء المتعلقة بحدود السمات وأمان الكائن","تحسين رمز روست للأداء bằng اختيار مستوى التمثيل الصحيح"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires knowledge of Rust programming language","Limited to addressing specific error codes like E0277 and E0308","Focus on Rust''s type system and trait bounds may not be directly applicable to other programming languages"],"zh":["需要Rust编程语言的知识","仅限于解决诸如E0277和E0308等特定错误代码","对Rust类型系统和特征边界的关注可能不直接适用于其他编程语言"],"ja":["Rustプログラミング言語の知識が必要","E0277およびE0308などの特定のエラーコードのみに対応","Rustの型システムと特性の境界への焦点は、他のプログラミング言語には直接適用できない可能性がある"],"ko":["Rust 프로그래밍 언어에 대한 지식이 필요함","E0277 및 E0308과 같은 특정 오류 코드만 해결함","Rust의 타입 시스템 및 특성 경계에 대한 중점은 다른 프로그래밍 언어에 직접 적용될 수 없음"],"es":["Requiere conocimiento del lenguaje de programación Rust","Limitado a abordar códigos de error específicos como E0277 y E0308","El enfoque en el sistema de tipos de Rust y los límites de rasgos puede no ser directamente aplicable a otros lenguajes de programación"],"fr":["Nécessite des connaissances en langage de programmation Rust","Limité à l''adresse de codes d''erreur spécifiques tels que E0277 et E0308","L''accent mis sur le système de types de Rust et les limites de traits peut ne pas être directement applicable à d''autres langages de programmation"],"de":["Benötigt Kenntnisse der Rust-Programmiersprache","Befasst sich nur mit der Behandlung spezifischer Fehlercodes wie E0277 und E0308","Der Fokus auf Rusts Typsystem und Trait-Grenzen kann möglicherweise nicht direkt auf andere Programmiersprachen angewendet werden"],"pt":["Requer conhecimento da linguagem de programação Rust","Limitado a abordar códigos de erro específicos, como E0277 e E0308","O foco no sistema de tipos do Rust e nos limites de traço pode não ser diretamente aplicável a outras linguagens de programação"],"ru":["Требует знания языка программирования Rust","Ограничен решением конкретных кодов ошибок, таких как E0277 и E0308","Фокус на системе типов Rust и ограничениях трейтов может не быть直接 применим к другим языкам программирования"],"ar":["يتطلب معرفة لغة البرمجة روست","محدود في معالجة رموز الخطأ الخاصة مثل E0277 و E0308","التركيز على نظام أنواع روست وحدود السمات قد لا يكون قابلا للتطبيق直接ا على لغات البرمجة الأخرى"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"3a2eed8faf0a0087aa5c823d66341123cc6f43ef36d1767c3fdbcc86cf8b4b54","qualityScore":0}');
